# Logs (structured, processed logs are tracked as the forensic audit trail;
# raw API cache is not). app.log is the exception: free-text, locally
# rotated/capped at 5MB x 3 backups (shared/utils/logger.py) — tracking it
# is redundant with those local backups and was producing large, noisy
# diffs that buried real code changes (2026-08-23 full model audit finding).
# The structured CSVs (audit_log/validation_log/override_log/performance_
# log/trade_outcomes/fill_log) stay tracked; only the free-text log doesn't.
data/logs/app.log*
data/raw/
data/historical/

# One-off ledger backups written before a schema migration or a retroactive
# correction (e.g. paper_trades.csv.pre-v2.2.105.bak). Local safety copies for
# the operator, not history worth carrying in the repo — the CHANGELOG entry
# for each migration records what changed, and the migrations themselves are
# idempotent and re-runnable. Added 2026-08-26 after a day of schema work left
# five of these in paper_trading/.
*.bak

# Desktop app UI — local scan history (App_UI_Scope.md), regenerated per machine
stockanalysis_history.db

# API-layer on-disk cache + rate-limiter state (shared/api_clients/cache.py, rate_limiter.py)
data/cache/

# V3 deep-analysis output (generated per run, not source)
reports/
